  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained ~5 mm N, ~11 mm U offset starting near index 508 (P1 onset), persisting through indices 508–549, then a sharp return at index 550 (P3) with opposite-signed offsets (~-4.6 mm N, ~-10.3 mm U), consistent with a temporary platform. P2 (index 545–546) is a 1-sample spike inconsistent with physical motion and not supported by surrounding observations; it likely reflects noise or artifact. Interior points (e.g., 510–549) show stable elevated levels in N and U, confirming a genuine temporary offset. The return at 550 is abrupt but physically plausible as a step-like recovery; no independent permanent step is evident within the interval. Thus only P1 and P3 form a coherent temporary platform pair.",
